{
  "id": "devops-232",
  "title": "Create and Configure the Auto Scaling Group in EC2 - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>AWS Auto Scaling automatically scales EC2 instances up or down based on incoming traffic demand. It helps reduce application latency and can be integrated with AWS services like</span><a href=\"#/article/devops/devops-214\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> Amazon DynamoDB</span></a><span> and </span><a href=\"#/article/devops/devops-218\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Amazon Aurora</span></a><span>.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"containerized_applications\" height=\"419\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522152940067162/containerized_applications.webp 1000w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522152940067162/containerized_applications-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522152940067162/containerized_applications-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522152940067162/containerized_applications-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522152940067162/containerized_applications-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522152940067162/containerized_applications-768.webp 768w\" width=\"1000\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"benefits-of-auto-scaling\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Benefits of Auto Scaling</span></h2><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Dynamic Scaling:</strong></b><span> Automatically scales applications up or down based on traffic demand.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Pay for What You Use:</strong></b><span> Optimizes resource usage and reduces unnecessary cost.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Automatic Performance Maintenance:</strong></b><span> Maintains application performance during workload changes.</span></li></ul><h2 id=\"how-aws-auto-scaling-works\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>How AWS Auto Scaling Working</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>AWS autoscaling will scale the application based on the load of application. Instead of scaling manually AWS auto scaling will scale the application automatically when the incoming traffic is high it will scale up the application and when the traffic is low it will scale down the application. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"AWS-AUTOSCALING\" height=\"279\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-2.png\" width=\"887\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span>First you should choose which service or an application you want to scale then select the optimization way like cost and performance and then keep track how the scaling is working. </span></p><h2 id=\"steps-to-create-auto-scaling-launch-template\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Steps To create Auto Scaling Launch Template</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><strong>Step 1: </strong></b><span>Click on the All Services on AWS Dashboard</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Click on the EC2(Elastic Cloud Computing).</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931\" height=\"483\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-3.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931.png 1437w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144356395785/Screenshot-2026-05-22-141931-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1437\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3: </strong></b><span>Scroll Down and click on the Launch Templates and click on the Create launch template</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033\" height=\"1141\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-4.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033.png 2849w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144504924334/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142033-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2849\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4: </strong></b><span>Type the Template name.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137\" height=\"799\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-5.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137.png 1919w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144507548765/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142137-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1919\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 5: </strong></b><span>Select the Amazon Machine Image.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245\" height=\"790\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-6.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245.png 1837w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144509667191/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142245-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1837\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 6: </strong></b><span>Select the Instance Type and</span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\"> </em></i><span>Key pair.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352\" height=\"983\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-7.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352.png 1879w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144510738373/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142352-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1879\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 7: </strong></b><span>Select the Security Group or Create the new one.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445\" height=\"866\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-8.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445.png 1816w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144734856966/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142445-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1816\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 8: </strong></b><span>Click on the Create Launch Template.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517\" height=\"914\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-9.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517.png 2798w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144818584458/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142517-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2798\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 9: </strong></b><span>Now you can see the template is created. Now, scroll down and click on the Auto Scaling Groups.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639\" height=\"1192\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-10.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639.png 2854w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522144904141303/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142639-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2854\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"create-an-auto-scaling-group-using-a-launch-template\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Create An Auto Scaling Group Using a Launch Template</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1: </strong></b><span>Click on the Create Auto Scaling group.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737\" height=\"872\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-11.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737.png 2874w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145013946764/Screenshot-2026-05-22-142737-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2874\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2: </strong></b><span>Type the Auto Scaling group name.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044\" height=\"1218\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-12.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044.png 2862w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145054405259/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143044-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2862\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3: </strong></b><span>Select your Template.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-13.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131.png 2116w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145057799144/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143131-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2116\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4: </strong></b><span>Select the VPC</span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\"> </em></i><span>or go with the default VPC and also select the Availability zone.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229\" height=\"924\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-14.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229.png 1582w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145058995194/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143229-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1582\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 5</strong></b><span>: Skip Integrate with other services</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 6:</strong></b><span> Configure the Group size and Scaling policies.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Select as per your requirement:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Desired: 4</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Minimum: 4</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Maximum: 8</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548\" height=\"1023\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-15.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548.png 1670w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145100137220/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143548-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1670\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 7: </strong></b><span>Select the Target tracking scaling policy.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654\" height=\"957\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-16.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654.png 2150w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145101369575/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143654-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2150\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 8: </strong></b><span>Click on the Create Auto Scaling Group.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442\" height=\"776\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-17.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442.png 2262w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145519805727/Screenshot-2026-05-22-145442-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2262\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Now you can see the Auto Scaling is creating and it is also creating the desired state of the EC2 Instance</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737\" height=\"375\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-18.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737.png 2761w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145102668429/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143737-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2761\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>We selected the Desired state equal to 4 and you can see the 4 Instance is Running</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917\" height=\"666\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-232-img-19.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917.png 2407w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260522145103408321/Screenshot-2026-05-22-143917-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"2407\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure></div>",
  "textContent": "AWS Auto Scaling automatically scales EC2 instances up or down based on incoming traffic demand. It helps reduce application latency and can be integrated with AWS services like Amazon DynamoDB and Amazon Aurora. Benefits of Auto ScalingDynamic Scaling: Automatically scales applications up or down based on traffic demand.Pay for What You Use: Optimizes resource usage and reduces unnecessary cost.Automatic Performance Maintenance: Maintains application performance during workload changes.How AWS Auto Scaling WorkingAWS autoscaling will scale the application based on the load of application. Instead of scaling manually AWS auto scaling will scale the application automatically when the incoming traffic is high it will scale up the application and when the traffic is low it will scale down the application. First you should choose which service or an application you want to scale then select the optimization way like cost and performance and then keep track how the scaling is working. Steps To create Auto Scaling Launch TemplateStep 1: Click on the All Services on AWS DashboardStep 2: Click on the EC2(Elastic Cloud Computing). Step 3: Scroll Down and click on the Launch Templates and click on the Create launch template Step 4: Type the Template name. Step 5: Select the Amazon Machine Image. Step 6: Select the Instance Type and Key pair. Step 7: Select the Security Group or Create the new one. Step 8: Click on the Create Launch Template. Step 9: Now you can see the template is created. Now, scroll down and click on the Auto Scaling Groups. Create An Auto Scaling Group Using a Launch TemplateStep 1: Click on the Create Auto Scaling group. Step 2: Type the Auto Scaling group name. Step 3: Select your Template. Step 4: Select the VPC or go with the default VPC and also select the Availability zone. Step 5: Skip Integrate with other servicesStep 6: Configure the Group size and Scaling policies.Select as per your requirement:Desired: 4Minimum: 4Maximum: 8 Step 7: Select the Target tracking scaling policy. Step 8: Click on the Create Auto Scaling Group. Now you can see the Auto Scaling is creating and it is also creating the desired state of the EC2 Instance We selected the Desired state equal to 4 and you can see the 4 Instance is Running",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/devops/create-and-configure-the-auto-scaling-group-in-ec2"
}
